#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:1
msgid "Upgrading to Mattermost Agents V2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:3
msgid ""
"This guide describes how to upgrade the Mattermost Agents plugin "
"(formerly Mattermost AI) from a v1.x release to v2.0.0. It covers the "
"supported version path, the migrations that run automatically on first "
"start of v2.0.0, the breaking changes and default-behavior flips that "
"admins should know about before the upgrade window, and the verification "
"steps to confirm the upgrade succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:5
msgid ""
"If you are running a fresh installation of v2.0.0 (no prior data, no "
"prior `config.bots` entries), you do not need this guide — install the "
"plugin and configure it using the [Admin Guide](admin_guide.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:7
msgid "1. Who this guide is for"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:9
msgid "You are the right reader if all of the following apply:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:11
msgid "You currently run the Mattermost AI / Mattermost Agents plugin at v1.x."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:12
msgid "You administer the Mattermost server (System Admin) and own its database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:13
msgid "You are planning to install v2.0.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:15
msgid ""
"If you are upgrading the Mattermost server itself, refer to the standard "
"Mattermost upgrade documentation in addition to this guide. The plugin "
"upgrade does not change Mattermost server requirements beyond those "
"listed in the [Admin Guide](admin_guide.md#prerequisites)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:17
msgid "2. Pre-flight checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:19
msgid ""
"Complete every item before starting the upgrade. Do not skip the database"
" backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:21
msgid ""
"**Confirm your current plugin version.** Go to **System Console > Plugin "
"Management** and note the installed version of Mattermost AI / Mattermost"
" Agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:22
msgid ""
"**Confirm your Mattermost server version.** v2.0.0 requires Mattermost "
"Server v10.0 or later. The optional external MCP HTTP server requires "
"Mattermost Server v11.2 or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:23
msgid ""
"**Back up the Mattermost database.** v2.0.0 runs schema migrations on "
"first start (see [Section 4](#4-what-gets-migrated-automatically)). Some "
"migrations are not safely reversible (see [Section 8](#8-rollback-"
"considerations)). In particular, migration 000007 drops the legacy "
"`LLM_PostMeta` table without migrating its contents into the new "
"conversation-entities tables — v1.x conversation titles cannot be "
"recovered after the upgrade except from this backup. See [Section 5](#5"
"-breaking-changes) for the full list of v1.x data that does not survive "
"the upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:24
msgid ""
"**Back up `config.json`.** The legacy bot migration removes entries from "
"stored plugin configuration after copying them into the database. Keeping"
" a pre-upgrade copy of `config.json` is the simplest way to recover "
"original bot definitions if you need to roll back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:25
msgid ""
"**Verify your license is current.** Multi-agent configurations, fine-"
"grained access controls, MCP support, and embedding search require an "
"Entry, Enterprise, or Enterprise Advanced license. See [License "
"requirements](/administration-guide/configure/agents-admin-guide.html"
"#license-requirements)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:26
msgid ""
"**Capture a list of currently configured bots.** From your existing "
"System Console > Plugins > Agents (or AI Bots) page, note the username, "
"display name, service binding, and access rules of each bot. After the "
"upgrade, you can compare this list against the migrated agents on the new"
" **Agents** product page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:27
msgid ""
"**Identify any external integrations that read the `LLM_PostMeta` table "
"directly.** That table is dropped by migration 000007. To our knowledge, "
"no documented integration depends on this table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:28
msgid ""
"**Schedule a maintenance window.** The plugin must be stopped and "
"restarted, and the migrations must complete before users resume traffic. "
"Typical windows in non-HA environments complete in minutes; HA clusters "
"should plan additional time for migration coordination (see [Section "
"9](#9-ha-specific-notes))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:30
msgid "3. Version sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:32
msgid ""
"The supported upgrade path is to upgrade Mattermost to the latest v11.6 "
"patch release before upgrading to Mattermost v11.7, which includes Agents"
" v2.0.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:34
msgid ""
"**Why this matters:** Mattermost v11.6 is the tested source release for "
"the Agents v2.0.0 upgrade. Upgrade to Mattermost v11.6 first if you are "
"running an earlier Mattermost or plugin version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:36
msgid "4. What gets migrated automatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:38
msgid ""
"When v2.0.0 starts for the first time on an existing install, the plugin "
"runs three database migrations and one in-process data migration. They "
"are coordinated for HA via cluster mutex and a system-table flag, and are"
" designed to be re-run safely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:40
msgid "4.1 Schema migrations (`store/migrations/`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Source PR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "`000005_create_user_agents_table`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "#589"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid ""
"Creates the `Agents_UserAgents` table that stores agent identity, "
"instructions, channel/user/team access lists, agent admins, MCP tool "
"grants, and lifecycle timestamps. Creates supporting indexes; index "
"creation is idempotent (PR #689)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "`000006_user_agent_bot_fields`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid ""
"Adds bot-specific columns to `Agents_UserAgents`: `Model`, "
"`EnableVision`, `DisableTools`, `EnabledNativeTools`, `ReasoningEnabled`,"
" `ReasoningEffort`, `ThinkingBudget`, `StructuredOutputEnabled`. "
"Backfills existing rows with `EnableVision=false`, `DisableTools=false`, "
"`ReasoningEnabled=true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "`000007_create_conversations_table`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "#602"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid ""
"Creates the `LLM_Conversations` and `LLM_Turns` tables that back the new "
"conversation-entities runtime. **Drops the legacy `LLM_PostMeta` table.**"
" Note: conversation titles stored in `LLM_PostMeta` from v1.x are not "
"automatically migrated; v2.0.0 builds its conversation history as users "
"interact with agents after the upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:48
msgid "4.2 Legacy bot migration (`server/legacy_bot_migration.go`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:50
msgid ""
"After the schema migrations run, the plugin performs a one-time migration"
" of legacy `config.bots` entries into `Agents_UserAgents`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:52
msgid ""
"The plugin acquires the cluster mutex `ai_legacy_bots_migration` so only "
"one node performs the migration in HA deployments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:53
msgid ""
"The plugin checks the `legacy_config_bots_migrated` flag in the "
"`Agents_System` table. If set, the migration is a no-op."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:54
msgid ""
"For each entry in `config.bots`, the plugin verifies that a corresponding"
" Mattermost bot account already exists. If any required Mattermost bot "
"row is missing, the migration is **deferred** without setting the "
"completion flag (it will retry on the next config update or restart)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:55
msgid "Each `config.bots` entry is copied into `Agents_UserAgents` with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:56
msgid "A new agent ID and timestamps assigned by the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:57
msgid "`BotUserID` linked to the existing Mattermost bot account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:58
msgid "`CreatorID` left empty (migrated agents do not have a creator)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:59
msgid "`AdminUserIDs` cleared. Migrated agents are managed by system admins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:60
msgid ""
"`AutoEnableNewMCPTools = true` so migrated agents preserve the v1.x "
"behavior of having access to every MCP tool, including ones added later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:61
msgid ""
"The plugin clears `config.bots` from stored configuration to prevent "
"duplicate bot registration on subsequent restarts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:62
msgid "The plugin sets `legacy_config_bots_migrated = true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:64
msgid "4.3 What changes in the System Console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:66
msgid ""
"**AI Bots** → redirects to the new top-level **Agents** product page. The"
" legacy AI Bots editor is replaced by the **Agents** management UI (list "
"page plus a three-tab agent editor: Configuration, Access, MCPs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:67
msgid ""
"**Enable MCP Client** and **Enable Embedded Server** toggles are removed "
"(PR #617). MCP and the embedded Mattermost MCP server are always on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:68
msgid ""
"The **Use Responses API** toggle is removed for the **OpenAI** service "
"type. OpenAI direct always uses the Responses API. The toggle remains for"
" **OpenAI Compatible** and **Azure OpenAI** services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:70
msgid "5. Breaking changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:72
msgid ""
"The following changes can affect deployments that depend on prior "
"behavior. Review each item before the upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:74
msgid "5.0 v1.x data that does not survive the upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:76
msgid ""
"The upgrade removes some v1.x data without migrating it forward. Confirm "
"your database backup is good before starting the procedure in [Section "
"7](#7-step-by-step-upgrade-procedure)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:78
msgid ""
"**v1.x conversation titles (`LLM_PostMeta` table contents).** Migration "
"000007 drops the `LLM_PostMeta` table without copying its rows into the "
"new `LLM_Conversations` / `LLM_Turns` schema. Conversation titles that "
"v1.x stored against root post IDs are not visible in v2.0.0 and cannot be"
" reconstructed from `LLM_Conversations` after the upgrade — restore from "
"the pre-upgrade database backup if you need that data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:80
msgid "5.1 `config.bots` is no longer the source of truth for agent definitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:82
msgid ""
"After the legacy bot migration runs, `config.bots` is cleared from stored"
" plugin configuration. Editing `config.json` to add or modify agents will"
" not have an effect — agent CRUD is now performed against "
"`Agents_UserAgents` via the **Agents** page. Any tooling that drives "
"agent definitions by writing to `config.bots` must be updated to call the"
" agent API or use the **Agents** page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:84
msgid "5.2 The `LLM_PostMeta` table is dropped"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:86
msgid ""
"Migration 000007 drops `LLM_PostMeta` after creating the new "
"`LLM_Conversations` and `LLM_Turns` tables. The drop runs without copying"
" row contents forward, so v1.x conversation titles stored in "
"`LLM_PostMeta` are not preserved (see [Section 5.0](#50-v1x-data-that-"
"does-not-survive-the-upgrade)). Any external integration that reads from "
"`LLM_PostMeta` will break after the upgrade. To our knowledge, no public "
"integration depends on this table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:88
msgid "5.3 MCP cannot be globally disabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:90
msgid ""
"The **Enable MCP Client** and **Enable Embedded Server** System Console "
"toggles are removed. To restrict MCP usage, disable individual tools or "
"change tool approval policies under **System Console > Plugins > Agents >"
" Model Context Protocol (MCP) > Tools**, or restrict an agent's MCP "
"access via the agent's **MCPs** tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:92
msgid "5.4 OpenAI direct always uses the Responses API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:94
msgid ""
"Services with type **OpenAI** unconditionally route through the OpenAI "
"Responses API. If you require legacy Chat Completions behavior, configure"
" an **OpenAI Compatible** service pointing at the OpenAI endpoint and "
"turn **Use Responses API** off for that service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:96
msgid "5.5 Standalone MCP server binary scope clarified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:98
msgid ""
"The standalone `mattermost-mcp-server` binary (separate process, stdio "
"transport) is documented as **development and local use only** and is not"
" supported in production deployments. Production environments should rely"
" on the embedded Mattermost MCP server and, when external clients are "
"required, the HTTP MCP server endpoint configured from the System "
"Console."
msgstr ""

