#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:148
msgid ""
"No fatal migration errors. If any error occurs, see [Section "
"11](#11-troubleshooting)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:149
msgid ""
"**Open the Agents page.** From the Mattermost product menu, navigate to "
"the top-level **Agents** product entry. Confirm that each agent you noted"
" in [Section 2 step 6](#2-pre-flight-checklist) is present. Migrated "
"agents have no creator listed; system admins can edit and delete them "
"from the row overflow menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:150
msgid "**Spot-check migrated agent configuration.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:151
msgid ""
"Open the agent. Confirm the **Configuration** tab shows the expected "
"display name, username, service, model, and custom instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:152
msgid ""
"Confirm the **Access** tab shows the channel, user, team, and admin "
"restrictions you expect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:153
msgid ""
"Confirm the **MCPs** tab shows **Automatically enable all MCP tools** "
"turned on (this preserves the v1.x behavior)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:154
msgid "**Re-enable user traffic.** End the maintenance window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:156
msgid "7.2 Secondary path: Upload the plugin bundle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:158
msgid ""
"Use this path only when you manage the Agents plugin bundle separately "
"from the Mattermost server package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:160
msgid ""
"**Take backups.** Back up the Mattermost database, `config.json`, and any"
" separate indexed-vector storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:161
msgid ""
"**Disable the plugin.** From **System Console > Plugin Management**, "
"locate **Mattermost AI** / **Mattermost Agents** and select **Disable**. "
"This prevents new traffic during the bundle swap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:162
msgid ""
"**Upload the v2.0.0 bundle.** Download the v2.0.0 plugin bundle "
"(`.tar.gz`) from the [GitHub releases page](https://github.com/mattermost"
"/mattermost-plugin-agents/releases). In **System Console > Plugin "
"Management**, select **Upload Plugin** and upload the bundle. If a "
"previous version is shown alongside the new bundle, remove the old "
"version after confirming the new one is selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:163
msgid ""
"**Re-enable the plugin.** Set the plugin to **Enabled**. On startup, "
"v2.0.0 runs migrations 000005, 000006, and 000007, then performs the "
"legacy bot migration described in [Section 4](#4-what-gets-migrated-"
"automatically)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:164
msgid ""
"**Complete the same post-upgrade checks.** Watch the logs, confirm "
"migrated agents are present, and spot-check migrated agent configuration "
"as described in [Section 7.1](#71-primary-path-upgrade-mattermost)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:166
msgid "8. Rollback considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:168
msgid ""
"Some v2.0.0 migrations cannot be cleanly reversed in production. Plan "
"accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Reversible?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Migration 000005 (`Agents_UserAgents` table)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Yes (drops table)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid ""
"Down migration drops the table and supporting indexes. Any agents created"
" or edited from the v2 UI between upgrade and rollback are lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Migration 000006 (bot fields on `Agents_UserAgents`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Yes (drops columns)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Down migration drops the added columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Migration 000007 (`LLM_Conversations`, `LLM_Turns`, drop `LLM_PostMeta`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "**Partial**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid ""
"Down migration drops `LLM_Conversations` and `LLM_Turns` and recreates an"
" empty `LLM_PostMeta`. `LLM_PostMeta` content (v1.x conversation titles) "
"cannot be recovered after migration 000007 drops the table — restore from"
" backup if you need that data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "Legacy bot migration (`config.bots` cleared)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid "**Manual**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md
msgid ""
"The v2 plugin clears `config.bots` after migration. To roll back, restore"
" the pre-upgrade `config.json` from your pre-flight backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:177
msgid "The supported rollback path is therefore:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:179
msgid "Disable the v2.0.0 plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:180
msgid "Restore the database from the pre-upgrade backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:181
msgid "Restore `config.json` from the pre-upgrade backup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:182
msgid "Reinstall the prior v1.x plugin bundle and re-enable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:184
msgid ""
"Do not attempt a rollback that runs only the down migrations — "
"`LLM_PostMeta` content (v1.x conversation titles) cannot be recovered "
"after migration 000007 drops the table; restore from backup if you need "
"that data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:186
msgid "9. HA-specific notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:188
msgid ""
"In HA deployments, complete the upgrade during a maintenance window and "
"allow the cluster to start normally. Agents coordinates the schema "
"migrations and legacy bot migration so only one node performs the data "
"migration work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:190
msgid ""
"After startup, check logs from all nodes for migration errors and confirm"
" the **Agents** page shows the expected migrated agents. If one node "
"reports migration errors while another node succeeds, stop the rollout, "
"preserve the logs, and contact Mattermost Support before retrying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:192
msgid "10. Verification checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:194
msgid "Tick through this list before ending the upgrade window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:196
msgid ""
"Plugin status in **System Console > Plugin Management** shows v2.0.0 "
"enabled with no errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:197
msgid ""
"Server logs show successful execution of migrations 000005, 000006, "
"000007."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:198
msgid ""
"Server logs show `Migrated legacy config bots to self-service agents "
"table` (or no legacy bots existed in the source install)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:199
msgid ""
"The top-level **Agents** product page is reachable from the Mattermost "
"product menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:200
msgid ""
"Every bot that existed in v1.x appears as an agent in the **Agents** list"
" with the same display name, username, and service binding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:201
msgid ""
"Editing a migrated agent shows the expected access rules and "
"**Automatically enable all MCP tools** turned on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:202
msgid ""
"**System Console > Plugins > Agents > AI Bots** redirects to the "
"**Agents** product page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:203
msgid ""
"**System Console > Plugins > Agents > Model Context Protocol (MCP)** does"
" not show **Enable MCP Client** or **Enable Embedded Server** toggles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:204
msgid ""
"Embedding search status (if previously enabled) shows healthy in **System"
" Console > Plugins > Agents > Embedding Search**, and any prior reindex "
"job is no longer stuck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:206
msgid "11. Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:208
msgid ""
"If the upgrade fails, stop the rollout and preserve the Mattermost server"
" logs from every node. Restore the database and `config.json` from the "
"pre-upgrade backups if you need to return service to the prior version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/docs/upgrading_to_2.0.md:210
msgid ""
"If migrations fail, the legacy bot migration does not complete, or "
"migrated agents do not appear on the **Agents** page after startup, "
"contact Mattermost Support with the server version, Agents plugin "
"version, migration log entries, and whether the deployment is single-node"
" or HA."
msgstr ""

